==French==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|fr}} {{m|frm|avec}}, {{m|frm|avecques||with}}, from {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{m|fro|avoc}}, {{m|fro|avoec}}, {{m|fro|avuec||with}}, from an assumed {{etyl|VL.|fr}} {{m|la|*aboc}}, {{m|la|*abhoc}}, {{m|la|*apud hŏque}},<ref>{{rfc|fr|year, edition, translator?}}
A. Brachet, ''An etymological dictionary of the French language'', avec.</ref><ref name=a>{{R:TLFi|etym=1}}</ref> a Frankish alteration consisting of {{etyl|la|fr}} {{m|la|apud||with, near, close to}} with {{m|la|hoc||this}} and {{m|la|-que}}. First used as a replacement for {{cog|la|cum||with}} in [[w:Merovingian|Merovingian]] and [[w:Carolingian|Carolingian]] (Frankish) documents. Gradually supplanted Old French {{m|fro|od||with}}, itself from {{m|la|apud}} (''od'' survives however in some dialects in Western France under the form ''d'ot'').<ref name=a/> 

Cognate with Picard {{m|pcd|avuc}}, Norman {{m|nrm|aveuc}}, Walloon {{m|wa|avou}} and, more distantly, with Franco-Provençal {{m|frp|avoi}} (from *''ab hoc'' and not *''abhocque'').

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA}}
* {{audio|fr|Fr-avec.ogg|audio}}

===Preposition===
{{fr-prep}}

# {{qualifier|accompaniment}} [[with]]
#: {{ux|fr|Je suis revenu '''avec''' lui.|t=I have returned '''with''' him.}}
#: {{ux|fr|Voudriez-vous y aller avec moi ?|Would you like to come with me?}}
# {{qualifier|manner, instrument}} [[with]]
#: {{ux|fr|Je l'ai fait avec plaisir.|I did that with pleasure.}}

